[StudyName "The Stalemate Gambit Explained"]
[ChapterName "05 · The royal walking tour"]
[TimeControl "180+0"]
[Source "https://lichess.org/rdt2NZGH"]

{ The founding game: mannyfresher against EmilioAsoXela, 3+0 blitz, 27 August 2026. Follow the king from his castle into the wilderness. The chapter pauses at story beats; the full legal game is here for replay. This is resourceful survival against missed wins, not a proven drawing opening. } 1. Nf3 d5 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. d3 e6 4. e3 Bb4 5. Bd2 O-O 6. Be2 Nc6 7. a3 Bxc3 8. Bxc3 e5 9. Qd2 d4 10. Bb4 Re8 11. O-O-O { 11.O-O-O: the king chooses the castle with the storm outside. Watch how quickly the shelter disappears. } 11... Nxb4 12. Qxb4 Qd5 13. e4 Qa2 14. Kd2 { 14.Kd2: King Ethelheim packs a sandwich and leaves home. } 14... b6 15. Rdg1 c5 16. Qb3 Qxb3 17. cxb3 Be6 18. b4 cxb4 19. a4 a5 20. Ng5 h6 21. Nxe6 Rxe6 22. g3 Rc8 23. h4 Rec6 24. f4 Rc2+ 25. Ke1 Rc1+ 26. Kf2 Rxg1 27. Rxg1 Rc2 28. fxe5 Nd7 29. g4 Rxb2 30. g5 hxg5 31. hxg5 Nxe5 32. g6 Nxg6 33. Rxg6 fxg6 { 33...fxg6: the last rook disappears. White now has a king, a bishop and pawns. The emergency plan is to stay in the game and make Black finish the job. } 34. Ke1 b3 35. Bg4 Rb1+ 36. Ke2 b2 37. e5 Rc1 38. Kf3 b1=Q { 38...b1=Q: a new dragon joins the chase. Black has a forced mate according to the source annotations, but must still execute it. } 39. e6 Qxd3+ 40. Kf4 Rf1+ 41. Ke5 Qe3+ 42. Kd6 Qf4+ 43. Kd7 Qxg4 44. Kd6 Rf6 45. Kc6 Qxe6+ 46. Kb5 { 46.Kb5: across the board again. Locate the checks and the escape squares before continuing. } 46... Rf5+ 47. Ka6 Qc6 48. Ka7 Rf7+ 49. Ka6 Qb7+ 50. Kb5 Rf5+ 51. Kc4 Qd5+ 52. Kd3 Qf3+ 53. Kc4 Rc5+ 54. Kxd4 Qd5+ 55. Ke3 Rc3+ 56. Kf4 Qe6 57. Kg5 Rg3+ 58. Kf4 Qg4+ 59. Ke5 Rf3 60. Kd5 Re3 61. Kc6 Qd4 62. Kb5 Rc3 63. Ka6 Qxa4 { 63...Qxa4: the final white pawn falls. From now on the king has no army to keep the game moving. } 64. Kb7 Qc6+ 65. Ka6 Qc8+ 66. Kb5 Rc5+ 67. Ka4 Rc4+ 68. Kb5 g5 69. Kxb6 g4 70. Kb5 g3 71. Kb6 g2 72. Kb5 g1=Q { 72...g1=Q: Black now has two queens, not three. The original queen and two promotions did not all survive: White captured the original queen on move 16. } 73. Kxa5 Qa7+ 74. Kb5 Qcb8+ 75. Kxc4 Qac7+ 76. Kd5 Qbd8+ 77. Ke6 Qce7+ 78. Kf5 Qdf8+ 79. Kg6 Qff6+ 80. Kh5 { 80.Kh5: one last square. Black can checkmate with Qf5, Qg5 or Qe2. The historical choice is one step away. } 80... Qee6 { 80...Qee6: safe, surrounded, immobile. Stalemate. The king has survived the entire expedition. } 1/2-1/2

